\id ZEC - Open English Translation—Readers’ Version (OET-RV) v0.2.12
\usfm 3.0
\ide UTF-8
\h Zechariah
\toc1 Zechariah
\toc2 Zechariah
\mt1 Zechariah
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\c 1
\s1 Israel urged to turn to Yahweh
\p
\v 1 In the eighth month of the second year of \add the reign of Persian King\add* Darius, Yahweh spoke through the prophet Zechariah \add Zechariah,\add* son of Ido’s son Berechiah) saying,
\v 2 “Yahweh was very angry with your ancestors,
\v 3 so tell \add this to\add* the people: Commander-in-chief Yahweh says that if you all turn back to me, I’ll return to you.
\v 4 Don’t be like your ancestors who’d been told by the prophets that Commander-in-chief Yahweh wanted them to abandon all their evil practices, but they wouldn’t listen or pay attention. That is Yahweh’s declaration.
\p
\v 5 “\add So\add* where are you ancestors and the prophets \add now\add*? Do they live forever?
\v 6 But your ancestors didn’t obey my words and my decrees that I commanded \add through\add* my servants the prophets, but they \add eventually\add* repented and said, ‘Commander-in-chief Yahweh has done to us just what our ways and actions deserved.’ ”
\s1 Yahweh’s compassion for Jerusalem
\p
\v 7 About three months later, Yahweh spoke again through the prophet Zechariah \add Zechariah\add* son of Ido’s son Berechiah) saying,
\v 8 “I had a vision in the night, and was surprised to see a man riding on a red horse, and then he was standing among the myrtle trees that are in the valley, and behind him there were red, reddish-brown, and white horses.”
\v 9 I asked, “What are these things, my master?”
\p Then that \add heavenly\add* messenger who talked with me told me, “I’ll show you what those things are.”
\p
\v 10 Then the man who stood among the myrtle trees answered and said, “Those are the ones that Yahweh has sent out to roam throughout the world.”
\p
\v 11 They answered Yahweh’s messenger who stood among the myrtle trees, telling him, “We’ve been roaming throughout the world, and see, the whole world sits contentedly and is at peace.”
\p
\v 12 “Commander-in-chief Yahweh,” Yahweh’s messenger asked, “how long before you show compassion to Jerusalem and to the cities of Judah, which you’ve been angry with for the past seventy years?”
\p
\v 13 Then that messenger who’d talked with me was answered by Yahweh with kind and comforting words,
\v 14 and that messenger told me, “Call out and say, ‘Commander-in-chief Yahweh says this: I’ve been very jealous for Jerusalem and for Zion.
\v 15 I’m very angry with the countries that are at ease—I was only a little angry with them, but they made the disaster worse.
\v 16 Therefore Yahweh says: I will show mercy Jerusalem again. My residence will be built within her, and the measuring line will be stretched out over her. That’s what Commander-in-chief Yahweh declares.
\p
\v 17 “Again, call out and say, ‘Commander-in-chief Yahweh says this: My cities will once again overflow with goodness, and I will again comfort Zion and choose Jerusalem.’ ”
\s1 The vision of the four horns
\p
\v 18 Then I looked up and wow, I saw four horns.
\v 19 I asked the messenger who’d talked with me, “What are those?”
\p “Those are the horns that have scattered Judah, Israel, and Jerusalem.” he answered.
\p
\v 20 Then Yahweh showed me four craftsmen
\v 21 and I asked, “What are those people coming to do?”
\p “Those horns are \add the nations\add* that scattered Judah so that everyone went into hiding,” he answered, “But the blacksmiths have come to terrify \add the horns\add*—to amputate the horns of the nations that attacked Judah, scattering the people.”
\c 2
\s1 The vision of Jerusalem expanded
\p
\v 1 Then I looked up, and wow, I saw a man holding a measuring line\f + \fr 2:1 \ft The modern equivalent would be a tape measure.\f*
\v 2 and I asked him, “Where are you going?”
\p “To measure Jerusalem,” he replied, “and to determine its width and length.”
\p
\v 3 Then to my surprise, the messenger who’d talked with me went away and another messenger went out to meet him
\v 4 and told him, “Run and speak to that young man, saying: Jerusalem won’t need city walls because there’ll be so many people and animals within it.
\v 5 Yahweh declares that he’ll become a wall of fire around it and will become the splendour in the middle of it.
\s1 Yahweh commands the exiles to go home
\p
\v 6 Yahweh declares: Get up and get moving. Flee from that land in the north, because I had scattered you into the four winds.
\v 7 \add Now\add* run you people who live in Babylon—escape to Zion.
\v 8 Commander-in-chief Yahweh said that, after he honoured and sent me against the nations that plundered you—
\q1 because anyone who touches you, is messing with God’s favourite.
\p
\v 9 \add He said,\add* “I myself will punish them, and they’ll be looted by their \add own\add* slaves.”
\p \add When you see that,\add* then you’ll know that Commander-in-chief Yahweh sent me.
\p
\v 10 Yahweh declares: “Sing and be glad, daughter of Zion, because I myself will come and settle among you.”
\p
\v 11 Then powerful nations will join Yahweh at that time, and they will become his people. He will settle among you, and you will know that Commander-in-chief Yahweh has sent me to you.
\v 12 Then Yahweh will inherit Judah as his rightful possession in that sacred region, and will once again choose Jerusalem.
\p
\v 13 All people everywhere, be silent before Yahweh, because from his sacred place, he’s been driven into action.
\c 3
\s1 Joshua and Satan
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh showed me the high priest Joshua standing in front of Yahweh’s messenger, and Satan was standing at his right to accuse him.
\v 2 But Yahweh told Satan, “May Yahweh rebuke you, Satan—may Yahweh who’s chosen Jerusalem, rebuke you. Isn’t \add he energetic like\add* a burning stick taken out of the fire?”
\p
\v 3 Now Joshua was dressed in filthy clothes as he stood in front of the messenger
\v 4 who told those standing in front of him, “Take off his filthy clothes.”
\p Then he said to Joshua, “Listen, I’ve taken away the guilt of your disobedience, and I’ll dress you in nice clothes.”
\p
\v 5 “Let them put a clean headband on his head,” I said, so they placed a clean headband on Joshua’s head and dressed him with \add new\add* clothes, while Yahweh’s messenger was standing \add there watching\add*.
\p
\v 6 Then he told Joshua,
\v 7 “Commander-in-chief Yahweh says: If you’ll follow my instructions and obey my rules, then you can govern my temple and guard my courtyards, because I’ll allow you to walk among these who are standing here.
\v 8 Please listen, Joshua the high priest, as well as your companions sitting in front of you. Those these men are a sign, because I myself will bring out my servant ‘the branch’.
\v 9 Now look at the stone that I’ve placed in front of Joshua—a single stone with seven faces \add cut on it\add*. Commander-in-chief Yahweh declares that I will engrave an inscription on it, and I will remove the sin from this land in one day.
\v 10 Commander-in-chief Yahweh declares that in that day, each man will invite his neighbour to sit under his grapevine or under his fig tree.”
\c 4
\s1 The container of lamp and the two olives
\p
\v 1 Then the messenger who was talking with me turned and woke me as if waking someone from their sleep.
\v 2 “What do you see?” he asked me.
\p “Wow,” I said, “I see a lampstand made entirely of gold, with a bowl on top of it. It has seven lamps on the top with a tube feeding each one,
\v 3 and two olive trees by it—one on each side of it.”
\v 4 Then I asked the messenger who was talking with me, “What are those, my master?”
\p
\v 5 “Don’t you know what those things mean?” he asked me.
\p “No, my master,” I replied.
\p
\v 6 So he told me, “This is Yahweh’s message to Zerubbabel: Commander-in-chief Yahweh says it won’t be my strength or my power, but with my spirit.
\v 7 What are you, big mountain? Before Zerubbabel you will become a plain. Then he will bring out the top stone to shouts of ‘Grace, grace to it.’ ”
\p
\v 8 Then Yahweh’s message \add came\add* to me, saying,
\v 9 “Zerubbabel’s hands have laid the foundation of this temple and his hands will bring it to completion.” Then you will have confirmation that Commander-in-chief Yahweh has sent me to you.
\v 10 Because who has mocked those who make a small difference? They will rejoice and will see Zerubbabel holding a plumb line.
\p Those seven \add lamps\add* are Yahweh’s eyes that roam over the whole world.
\p
\v 11 “What are these two olive trees on the right and left of the lampstand?” I asked the messenger.
\v 12 “And what are these two olive branches beside the two gold pipes that have golden oil pouring out of them?”
\p
\v 13 Then he answered, “Don’t you know what those are?”
\p “No, my master,” I replied.
\p
\v 14 Then he said, “Those are the two anointed men\f + \fr 4:14 \ft It’s not clear who this is referring to.\f* who stand before the master of the whole world.”
\c 5
\s1 The flying scroll vision
\p
\v 1 Then I turned around and looked up, and wow, I saw a flying scroll,
\v 2 and the messenger asked me, “What do you see?”
\p “I see a flying scroll,” I answered, “that’s nine metres long and half that wide.”
\p
\v 3 Then he told me, “That’s the curse that goes out over the surface of the whole land. Every thief will be removed according to what it says on the one side, and everyone who testifies falsely will be removed according to what it says on the other side.
\v 4 Commander-in-chief Yahweh declares: I will send it out so it will enter into the house of any thief and into the house of anyone who testified falsely using my name, and it will remain in that house and eat away at its timber and its stones.”
\s1 The woman in a basket vision
\p
\v 5 Then the messenger who’d been talking with me came over and said to me, “Look up and see what’s coming now.”
\p
\v 6 “What is it?” I asked.
\p And he said, “That’s the measuring bin that’s coming.” Then he continued, “That’s their eye\f + \fr 5:6 \ft Some ancient translations have ‘iniquity’ here, but we’ve stayed with the Hebrew.\f* across the whole land.”
\p
\v 7 Then, wow, a lead covering was lifted off and there was a woman sitting inside the measuring bin.
\v 8 He said, “This woman is ‘wickedness’.” Then he pushed her \add back\add* inside the measuring bin, then \add quickly\add* pressed the heavy lead \add cover back\add* over its opening.
\p
\v 9 Then I looked up \add again\add* and wow, I saw two women with wings like stork’s wings, flying on the wind towards us, and they lifted the measuring bin up into the sky.
\p
\v 10 “Where are they taking the measuring bin?” I asked the messenger who’d been talking with me.
\p
\v 11 “To build a temple for it in Babylon,” he replied. “And when it’s ready, it’ll be set on a base there.”
\c 6
\s1 The four chariots vision
\p
\v 1 Then I turned and looked up and wow, I saw four chariots coming out from between two bronze mountains.
\v 2 The first chariot \add was being pulled by\add* red horses, the second by black horses,
\v 3 the third by white horses, and the fourth by spotted grey horses.
\p
\v 4 I asked the messenger who had talked with me, “What are those, my master?”
\v 5 “Those are four winds of the heavens that go out from where they were, ahead of the master of the whole world,” he answered.
\v 6 “The chariot pulled by black horses will go north, the one pulled by white horses will go west, and the one pulled by spotted grey horses will go south.”
\v 7 The strong \add horses\add* went out and wanted to go and roam over the earth, and he said, “Go and roam over the earth.” and they went to roam over the earth.
\v 8 Then the messenger called out and told me, “Look at the ones that are going out to the north country. They will appease my spirit in the north country.”
\s1 The crowning of Joshua
\p
\v 9 Then Yahweh’s message \add came\add* to me, saying,
\v 10 “Take \add the offering\add* from the exiles that Helday, Toviyah, and Yedayah \add are bringing\add*, and go this same day and take it into Josiah’s house (Zephaniah’s son, who has come from Babylon.
\v 11 Then take the gold and silver, and make a crown and place it on the head of the high priest, Joshua Yehotsadak’s son)
\v 12 and tell him, ‘Commander-in-chief Yahweh says:
\m Look, a man whose name is ‘Branch’ will grow from his place, and he will build Yahweh’s temple.
\v 13 Yes, he will build Yahweh’s temple, and he will radiate splendour and will sit and rule on his throne. He’ll be a priest on his throne, and peace will emanate from the interaction of both of those roles.
\v 14 Then the crown will be given to Helday, to Toviyah, to Yedayah, and to Zephaniah’s son Hen as a memorial in Yahweh’s temple.
\p
\v 15 Then those live far away will come and build Yahweh’s temple, so you will know that Commander-in-chief Yahweh has sent me to you. \add All\add* that will happen if you truly listen to the voice of your god Yahweh.’ ”
\c 7
\s1 Fasting with wrong motivation
\p
\v 1 On the 4th of the ninth month (\add named\add* ‘Kislev’) in the fourth year of the reign of \add Persian\add* King Darius, Yahweh’s message came to Zechariah.
\p
\v 2 The \add people of\add* Bethel had sent Sharetser and Regem-Melek and their men to request prayers for Yahweh’s favour.
\v 3 They asked the priests who were at Commander-in-chief Yahweh’s temple, along with the prophets, “Should I fast in the fifth month to show that I’m mourning, as I’ve been doing for many years?”
\p
\v 4 So Commander-in-chief Yahweh’s message came to me:
\v 5 “Ask the priests and the people all over the country, ‘When you fasted and mourned in the fifth and seventh months for \add the past\add* seventy years, were you truly fasting for me?
\v 6 When you ate and drank \add together\add*, weren’t you yourselves just enjoying the food and drink?
\v 7 Weren’t those the same words that Yahweh declared through the former prophets, when you still inhabited Jerusalem and the surrounding cities in prosperity and were settled in the Negev, and the western foothills?’ ”
\s1 Exile follows disobedience
\p
\v 8 Then Yahweh’s message came to Zechariah:
\v 9 “Commander-in-chief Yahweh says, ‘Judge with true justice, loyal commitment, and mercy. Let everyone do that for their neighbour.
\v 10 Don’t oppress widows or orphans, foreigners or poor people, and none of you should plot any harm against another person, \add even\add* in your mind.’
\p
\v 11 But they refused to pay attention, turning away stubbornly and blocking their ears so they couldn’t hear.
\v 12 They made their hearts as hard as rock so they couldn’t hear the \add written\add* law or Commander-in-chief Yahweh’s \add contemporary\add* messages. He’d sent those messages to the people by his spirit in earlier times through the words of the prophets, but the people refused to listen, so Commander-in-chief Yahweh was very angry with them.
\v 13 And so it was that when he called, they didn’t listen. In the same way,” said Commander-in-chief Yahweh, “they’ll call out to me \add for help\add*, but I won’t listen.
\v 14 I’ll use a whirlwind to scatter them to other nations that they’ve never been to before. Then the land \add here\add* will become desolate after they’ve gone because no one will pass through this land or return to it since the people have made their pleasant country into a wasteland.”
\c 8
\s1 The promise to bless Jerusalem
\p
\v 1 Then Commander-in-chief Yahweh’s message \add came to me\add*, saying:
\v 2 “Commander-in-chief Yahweh says: I’m passionate for Zion with dedicated zeal and I am passionate for her with fierce anger.
\v 3 Commander-in-chief Yahweh says: I will return to Zion and will live in the middle of Jerusalem, because Jerusalem will be called ‘The city of truth’ and Commander-in-chief Yahweh’s mountain will be called ‘The sacred mountain’.
\v 4 Commander-in-chief Yahweh says:
\q1 Old men and old women will appear around Jerusalem’s streets once again,
\q1 and the people will need staffs in their hands because they’ve grown so old.
\v 5 The city streets will be full of children playing in them.
\p
\v 6 Commander-in-chief Yahweh says:
\q1 If something seems impossible in the eyes of the remnant of this people in those days,
\q1 Yahweh’s declaration is: ‘It doesn’t mean that it’s impossible for me.’
\v 7 Army command Yahweh says:
\q1 Listen, I’m about to rescue my people from the lands to the east and to the west,\f + \fr 8:7 \ft including Babylon in the east, and Egypt in the west.\f*
\v 8 and I’ll bring them back. Then they’ll live in the middle of Jerusalem, so they will be my people \add again\add* and I’ll be their god in truth and in righteousness.
\p
\v 9 Commander-in-chief Yahweh says:
\q1 “Let your hands be strong, all you who now hear these words spoken by the prophets who were present when the foundations were laid to rebuild the temple—Commander-in-chief Yahweh’s residence.
\v 10 Because before those days, no crops were gathered in by anyone. There was no profit for either man or animal, and there was no peace from enemies for anyone going or coming. I had caused every person to be against their neighbours.
\v 11 But now it won’t be like it was in times past. Commander-in-chief Yahweh declares that I’ll be with the remnant of this people.
\v 12 Because seeds of peace \add will be sown\add*. The grapevine will produce its fruit and the soil will give its produce. The skies will give their dew, because I’ll give all those things to those people as an inheritance.
\v 13 House of Judah and house of Israel, you were \add made into\add* an example of a curse for the other nations \add to see\add*. So I will rescue you and you’ll be a blessing. Don’t be afraid—work hard \add to finish building the temple\add*.
\p
\v 14 Because Commander-in-chief Yahweh says: Just as I didn’t relent when I’d planned to do harm to you all when your ancestors provoked my anger,
\v 15 so also at this time I’ll plan to do good again to Jerusalem and the house of Judah. Don’t be afraid.
\v 16 These are the things that you all must do: \add Always\add* tell the truth to those around you. Judge with truth, justice, and peace in your community courts.
\v 17 Yahweh declares: Don’t inwardly plan to do evil things to others around you all, and don’t encourage false testimonies because those are the things I hate.”
\p
\v 18 Then Commander-in-chief Yahweh’s message came to me, saying,
\v 19 “Commander-in-chief Yahweh says this: The fasts of the fourth month, the fifth month, the seventh month, and the tenth month will become times of joy, gladness, and happy festivals for the house of Judah. Therefore appreciate and strive for truth and peace.
\p
\v 20 Commander-in-chief Yahweh says: People will come again, even those who are \add currently\add* living in various different cities.
\v 21 The inhabitants of one city will go to another city and say, ‘Let’s go quickly \add to Jerusalem\add* to make our requests to Yahweh—to ask for the favour of Commander-in-chief Yahweh. We ourselves are also going.’
\v 22 Many people and powerful nations will come to seek Commander-in-chief Yahweh \add there\add* in Jerusalem, and to beg for Yahweh’s favour.
\v 23 Commander-in-chief Yahweh says: In those days, ten men from every language and nation will grasp the hem of your robe and say, ‘Let us go with you, because we’ve heard that God helps you.’ ”
\c 9
\s1 The punishment of Israel’s enemies
\p
\v 1 This is a declaration of Yahweh’s message concerning the \add Syrian\add* Hadrak region and \add focusing on\add* Damascus \add city\add*, because the eyes of all humanity, including all of Israel’s tribes, are toward Yahweh.
\v 2 It’s also \add about\add* the Hamat \add region which\add* borders on Tyre and Sidon which is very wise.
\v 3 Tyre has built herself a fortress and heaped up silver like dust and refined gold like mud in the streets.
\v 4 Listen, my master will dispossess her and throw her wealth into the sea, and she’ll be consumed by fire.
\p
\v 5 Ashkelon \add city\add* will see and be afraid. Gaza \add city (Gaza)\add* will also squirm in pain. Ekron \add city\add* will have her hopes dashed. Gaza’s king will die, and Ashkelon will no longer be inhabited.
\v 6 Strangers will move into Ashdod, and I’ll end the Philistines’ pride.
\v 7 I will remove the meat with blood still in it from their mouths and their \add foods offered to idols\add* from between their teeth. Then they’ll become a remnant for our god like a clan in Judah, and Ekron will end up like the Jebusites \add did\add*.
\v 8 I’ll camp around my house as a guard to prevent anyone from passing through or returning so no oppressor can overrun them, because I’ve now looked with my own eyes.
\s1 Zion’s coming king
\q1
\v 9 Shout with a huge celebration, daughter of Zion.
\q1 Shout with happiness, Jerusalem’s daughter.
\q1 Look! Your king is coming to you bringing justice and victory.
\q1 He’s humble and is riding on a donkey, i.e., a donkey’s foal.
\q1
\v 10 Then I’ll neutralise the chariots heading to Israel,
\q1 and the horses heading to Jerusalem,
\q1 and the bows won’t make it into battle.
\q1 He’ll speak peace to the nations,
\q1 and his dominion will be from sea to sea,
\q1 and from the Euphrates to the ends of the earth.
\s1 The rescue of God’s people
\q1
\v 11 You \add people of Jerusalem\add*, because of the blood of my agreement with you,
\q1 I’ll set your prisoners free from that pit without water in it.
\q1
\v 12 You prisoners with hope, return back inside the walls.
\q1 Even today I’m declaring that I will return double to you,
\q1
\v 13 because I’ve bent Judah as my bow.
\q1 I have filled my quiver with Israel.
\q1 Zion, I’ve roused your sons, against your sons, Greece,
\q1 and Zion, I’ve made you like a warrior’s sword.”
\q1
\v 14 Then Yahweh will appear to them,
\q1 and his arrow will shoot out like lightning,
\q1 because my master Yahweh will sound the trumpet
\q1 and will advance with the storms from the south.
\q1
\v 15 Commander-in-chief Yahweh will defend them,
\q1 and they will devour them and deflect the stones from the slings.
\q1 Then they’ll drink and shout like men drunk on wine,
\q1 and they’ll be filled with wine like bowls,
\q2 \add drenched\add* like the corners of the altar.
\b
\q1
\v 16 Then on that day, their god Yahweh will rescue them,
\q2 as the flock of his people.
\q1 They’re the jewels of a crown that will sparkle over his land.
\q1
\v 17 How good and how beautiful they’ll be.
\q1 The young men will flourish on grain
\q1 and the young women on new wine!
\c 10
\s1 Judah and Israel will be rescued
\q1
\v 1 Ask Yahweh for rain in the springtime—
\q1 Yahweh who makes thunderstorms and gives rain showers to everyone
\q1 \add including the\add* vegetation in the countryside.
\q1
\v 2 Diviners tell deceitful dreams and give empty comfort
\q1 because household idols speak falsely and \add so\add* those diviners envision \add something that’s\add* a lie.
\q1 →Therefore the people wander like sheep and suffer because there’s no shepherd.
\p
\v 3 “I’m angry with the shepherds—it’s the leaders that I’ll punish.
\q1 Commander-in-chief Yahweh will also attend to his flock—the house of Judah,
\q1 and make them like his warhorse in battle.
\q1
\v 4 The \add building’s\add* cornerstone will come from Judah.
\q1 From him will come the tent peg,
\q1 from him will come the war bow,
\q1 from him will come every one of their strong leaders.
\q1
\v 5 They’ll be like warriors in battle
\q1 who trample their enemies into the mud of the streets.
\q1 They’ll go to war, because Yahweh is with them,
\q1 and they’ll shame those riding warhorses.
\b
\q1
\v 6 I’ll strengthen the house of Judah
\q1 and save the house of Joseph
\q1 because I’ll bring them back and have compassion on them.
\q1 They’ll be as though I hadn’t driven them off,
\q1 because I’m their god Yahweh,
\q1 and I’ll respond to them.
\q1
\v 7 Then Israel will be like a warrior,
\q1 and their hearts will rejoice as with wine;
\q1 Their children will see and rejoice.
\q1 Their hearts will rejoice in me!
\b
\q1
\v 8 I’ll whistle \add to call\add* them and gather them,
\q1 because I’ll rescue them,
\q1 and they’ll become as numerous as they were previously.
\q1
\v 9 I scattered them among the nations,
\q1 ^but they’ll remember me in distant countries,
\q1 →so they and their children will live and return,
\q1
\v 10 because I’ll bring them back from Egypt
\q1 and gather them from Assyria.
\q1 I’ll bring them to Gilead and Lebanon
\q1 until the region is filled with them.
\b
\q1
\v 11 Yahweh will lead them through their sufferings.
\q1 He will strike the waves of that sea
\q1 and will dry up all the depths of the Nile.
\q1 The Assyria’s greatness will come to an end,
\q1 and Egypt’s power will be removed.
\q1
\v 12 I will strengthen them in myself,
\q1 and they will obey what I’ve instructed them.
\q1 That is Yahweh’s declaration.”
\c 11
\s1 The punishment of Lebanon and Bashan
\q1
\v 1 Open your doors, Lebanon,
\q1 →so that fire can devour your cedar trees.
\q1
\v 2 Wail, cypress trees, because the cedar trees have fallen.
\q1 What was majestic has been devastated.
\q1 Wail, you Bashan oaks, because the strong forest has come down.
\q1
\v 3 Listen to the shepherds wail,
\q1 because their pride and joy has been destroyed.
\q1 Listen to the young lions roaring,
\q1 because the pride of the Jordan \add river\add* has been devastated.
\s1 The two shepherds
\p
\v 4 My god Yahweh says: “Be like a shepherd who’s watching over the flock that have been marked to be slaughtered.
\v 5 The ones who buy them, slaughter them and aren’t punished, and the ones who sell them say, ‘Blessed be Yahweh. I’ve become rich.’ because the shepherds working for the flocks’ owners have no pity on them.
\p
\v 6 This is Yahweh’s declaration: I will no longer feel sorry for the people of this country. Listen, I’m about to allow everyone to be taken over by their neighbours and by their king and \add allow them to\add* destroy the land, and I won’t rescue anyone from them.”
\p
\v 7 So I became the shepherd of the flock that had been marked for slaughter—the ones who were suffering the most. I took two \add shepherd’s\add* staffs—I named one ‘Favour’, and the other I named ‘Unity’, and then I shepherded the flock.
\v 8 Then I destroyed the three shepherds—in one month I became impatient with them, and they also hated me.
\v 9 So I said to the owners, “I won’t work for you any longer as a shepherd. The sheep that are dying—let them die. The sheep that are being destroyed—let them be destroyed. Let the sheep that remain start eating each other.”
\p
\v 10 Then I took my staff \add named\add* ‘Favour’ and broke it to break the agreement that I’d made with all of my tribes.
\v 11 So the agreement was broken on that day, and the ones in the flock who were suffering the most and who were watching me, knew that Yahweh had spoken.
\v 12 Then I told them, “If it seems good to you, give me my wages, but if not, don’t bother.” So they paid me thirty silver coins.
\p
\v 13 Then Yahweh told me, “Give the money to the potter\f + \fr 11:13 \ft potter (following the Hebrew): in the ancient Syriac translation, they used ‘treasury’ (2x) in this verse, so some other English translations might differ.\f*—the pathetic amount that they valued you at.” So I took the thirty silver coins and tossed them to the potter in Yahweh’s temple.
\v 14 Then I broke my second staff \add named\add* ‘Unity’ to break the brotherhood between Judah and Israel.
\p
\v 15 After that, Yahweh told me, “Again, take the equipment of a simple shepherd for yourself,
\v 16 because listen, I’m about to set a shepherd in place in the land who won’t care for those who are dying. He won’t seek out the sheep gone missing, nor will he heal the crippled sheep. He won’t feed the sheep that are healthy, but he’ll tear off the hooves of the fattened sheep and eat them for meat.
\q1
\v 17 The worthless shepherd who abandons the flock won’t end well.
\q1 May the sword come against his arm and his right eye.
\q1 May his arm wither away and may his right eye become blind.”
\c 12
\s1 Jerusalem’s protection
\p
\v 1 This is a declaration of Yahweh’s message concerning Israel—a declaration of Yahweh, who stretched out the skies and laid the foundation of the earth, who forms the human spirit that’s inside people,
\v 2 “Listen, I’m about to make Jerusalem into a cup causing all the nations surrounding her to stagger around. It will also be like that for Judah during the siege against Jerusalem.
\v 3 At that time, I’ll make Jerusalem into a heavy stone for all the peoples. Anyone trying to lift that stone will hurt himself very much, and all the nations in the world will gather against that city.
\v 4 This is Yahweh’s declaration: At that time, I will strike every horse with confusion and its rider with madness. I’ll open my eyes over the Judah region, but I’ll strike every horse from other countries with blindness.
\v 5 Then the leaders of Judah will say to themselves, ‘The inhabitants of Jerusalem are our strength because of their god, Commander-in-chief Yahweh.’
\p
\v 6 At that time, I will make the leaders of Judah like firepots among wood and like a flaming torch among standing grain, because they’ll devour all the surrounding peoples on their right and on their left. Jerusalem will again live in her own place.”
\s1 Saving Jerusalem’s inhabitants
\p
\v 7 Yahweh will save Judah’s tents first, so that the honour of David’s descendants and the honour of Jerusalem’s inhabitants won’t be greater than the rest of Judah.
\v 8 At that time, Yahweh will be the defender of the inhabitants of Jerusalem. Those among them who are weak will become \add strong\add* like David, while David’s descendants will be like God, like Yahweh’s messenger going ahead of them.
\v 9 “On that day I will begin to destroy all the nations that fight against Jerusalem.”
\p
\v 10 But I will pour out a spirit of compassion and pleading on David’s descendants and the inhabitants of Jerusalem, so they will look on me—the one they’ve pierced. They’ll mourn for me, as one mourns for an only son—they will wail bitterly for him like those who wail after the death of a firstborn son.
\v 11 On that day the wailing in Jerusalem will be like the wailing at Hadad-Rimon in the Megiddo plain.
\v 12 The land will mourn, each clan separate from other clans. The clan of David’s descendants will be separate and their wives will be separate from the men. The clan of Nathan’s descendants will be separate and their wives will \add also\add* be separate from the men.
\v 13 The clan of Levi’s descendants will be separate and their wives will be separate from the men. The clan of the Shim’im will be separate and their wives will \add also\add* be separate from the men.
\v 14 Each of the remaining clans will be separate and the wives will be separate from the men.”
\c 13
\s1 The cleaning of sins from Israel
\p
\v 1 “On that day a spring will be opened for David’s descendants and the \add other\add* inhabitants of Jerusalem, \add to clean them from\add* their sin and impurity.
\p
\v 2 This is the declaration of Commander-in-chief Yahweh: That \add same\add* day, I will eliminate the names of the idols from the country and then no one will be able to remember them. I’ll remove the \add false\add* prophets and the spirit of impurity from the land.
\v 3 If anyone continues to prophesy, his father and mother will tell him, ‘You can’t be allowed to live because you speak lies using Yahweh’s name’ Then the \add very\add* father and mother who gave birth to him will run him through when he prophesies.
\v 4 At that time, each prophet will become ashamed of his vision when he is about to prophesy, \add so\add* in order to deceive \add the people\add*, these prophets won’t put on a hairy cloak any more,
\v 5 and they’ll \add each\add* say, ‘I’m not a prophet. I’m a man who works the soil—I’ve been doing that since I was young.’
\v 6 But \add someone\add* will ask him, ‘What are these wounds between your arms?’ and he’ll answer, ‘I got \add accidentally\add* wounded in my friends’ house.’ ”
\s1 The shepherd gets attacked
\p
\v 7 Army command Yahweh declares:
\q1 Wake up, sword, \add and work\add* against \add the one who’s\add* my shepherd and the man who stands close to me.
\q1 Strike the shepherd and the flock will scatter
\q1 because I’ll turn my hand against the lowly ones.
\q1
\v 8 Yahweh declares: Then it’ll come about that throughout all the land,
\q1 that two-thirds of it will be cut off.
\q1 Those people will die—only one-third will remain there.
\q1
\v 9 I’ll bring that third through the fire and refine them like silver is refined.
\q1 I’ll test them like gold is tested.
\q1 They will call out to me for help,
\q1 and I’ll answer them saying, ‘This is my people.’
\q1 and they’ll say, ‘Yahweh is my god.’ ”
\c 14
\s1 God appears and reigns
\p
\v 1 Listen, a day is coming for Yahweh, when your plunder will be divided right in front of you,
\v 2 because I will assemble every country to battle against Jerusalem and the city will be captured. The houses will be plundered and the women raped. Half of the city will be led away into captivity, but the remainder of the people won’t be evicted from the city.
\v 3 Then Yahweh will go out and fight against those nations like when he fights on the day of battle.
\v 4 On that day, his feet will stand on the Mt. of Olives, which is just east of Jerusalem. The Mt. of Olives will be split in half between the east and the west by a very great valley, and half of the mountain will go back toward the north and half toward the south.
\v 5 Then you all will flee down the valley between Yahweh’s mountains, because the valley between those mountains will reach to Atsel. You will flee just like you fled from the earthquake in the days of Judah’s King Uzziah. Then my god Yahweh will come and all the holy ones will be with him.
\v 6 On that day, there’ll be no light—precious things will freeze together.
\v 7 On that day (known only to Yahweh), there’ll no longer be day or night, because it’ll stay light at ‘night’.
\p
\v 8 On that day, living waters will flow out of Jerusalem. Half of them will flow to the Dead sea and half to the Mediterranean sea, \add both\add* in summer and in winter.
\v 9 Yahweh will be king over all the world. On that day there will \add only\add* be Yahweh, the one God—no other gods.
\p
\v 10 All the land will be like the plain from Geva to Rimon south of Jerusalem. Jerusalem will continue to be in the hills and remain in its own place, from the Benjamin gate to the place where the first gate was, to the Corner gate, and from the Hananel tower to the king’s wine-pressing \add pits\add*.
\v 11 It’ll be inhabited and never \add completely\add* destroyed again—Jerusalem will live in security.
\p
\v 12 The deadly disease that Yahweh will use to attack all the nations that fought against Jerusalem will be that their flesh will rot away even while they’re \add still\add* standing on their feet. Their eyes will rot in their sockets and their tongues will rot in their mouths.
\p
\v 13 On that day, Yahweh will cause them to panic—they’ll grab hold of each other, and then they’ll start attacking each other.
\v 14 Judah will also fight against Jerusalem, and the wealth (gold, silver, and clothing) from all the surrounding countries will be collected \add together\add*.
\p
\v 15 That deadly disease will also affect the horses and mules, the camels and donkeys, and all the other animals in those camps.
\p
\v 16 After that, all who remain in those nations that came against Jerusalem will instead go up from year to year to worship the king (Commander-in-chief Yahweh), and to observe the celebration in shelters.
\v 17 It will happen that if anyone from all the countries in the world doesn’t go to Jerusalem to worship the king (Commander-in-chief Yahweh) then Yahweh won’t send them any rain.
\v 18 If Egypt doesn’t go, then they won’t get any rain. A deadly disease from Yahweh will attack the nations that do not go to Jerusalem to observe the celebration in shelters.
\v 19 That will be the punishment for Egypt and the punishment for every country that doesn’t go to observe that celebration in shelters.
\p
\v 20 On that day, the horses’ bells will say, “Dedicated to Yahweh,” and the basins in Yahweh’s residence will be like the bowls in front of the altar,
\v 21 because every pot in Jerusalem and Judah will be dedicated to Commander-in-chief Yahweh and everyone who brings a sacrifice will eat from them and boil in them. On that day, there will no longer be any traders in Commander-in-chief Yahweh’s residence.
